===== CAPTION TEXT =====
A: Figure 24: Unfolded data and MINERvA Tune v1 (GENIE 2.12.6 with analysis tune weights, the OmniFold prior) in (Eavail , W ). Top gives dimensionless per-cell data/Tune on a 0.5–1.5 colour scale; bottom gives per-cell data − Tune in units of 10−40 cm2 /nucleon. Equal-size display cells are labelled by physical bin edges on the 7×6 reporting grid, with Eavail edges [0, 0.1, 0.2, 0.4, 0.8, 1.5, 3.0, 100] GeV and W edges [0, 1.1, 1.4, 1.8, 2.2, 3.0, 100] GeV. The final interval on each axis, [3, 100] GeV, is a wide catch bin. The density ratio is independent of cell area; the bottom panel instead subtracts cell-integrated cross sections, (d2 σ/dEavail dW ) × ∆Eavail ∆W in cm2 /nucleon, so the catch-bin cells, which are wide, carry correspondingly larger values. Together the panels locate the positive excess at high Eavail and high W , with a secondary component at W < 1.1 GeV and a small deficit at W ≃ 1.4–1.8 GeV. Quoted percentage shares refer to cell-integrated positive excess in the bottom panel.
B: FIG. 3. Efficiency for the νµ CC inclusive signal in bins of muon longitudinal and transverse momentum. The efficiency is highest (> 85%) for high p|| and low pT , corresponding to good acceptance into the MINOS ND.
